sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant B as Browser
    participant NX as nginx
    participant U as handleUpgrade
    participant L as lifecycle.open
    participant R as Redis

    B->>NX: GET /ws  Upgrade: websocket
    NX->>NX: geo check → 451 if EEA/UK
    NX->>U: proxied
    U->>U: path check → 404
    U->>U: draining? → 503 shutting_down
    U->>U: accountId := auth.accountForRequest(cookie)   [null if signed out]
    U->>U: origin allowlist → 403
    U->>U: presented := resume subprotocol (presence only)
    U->>U: admission(registry.size, max, reserve)
    Note over U: full → 503 · reserved && no token → 503<br/>Both return the IDENTICAL 503 (naming the reserve<br/>would tell a client what to claim to be)
    U->>U: address = clientAddress(req, TRUST_PROXY_HOPS)<br/>country = CF-IPCountry<br/>ipHash, clientHash = salted sha256
    U->>R: checkBan(ipHash, clientHash)
    Note over U: Redis error here → 503, NOT admit
    alt banned
        U-->>B: 403 forbidden (no detail about which dimension)
    end
    U->>L: open(ipHash, clientHash, beforeCreate)
    L->>R: connRateLimit(ipHash)
    L->>L: sessionId = newSessionId()  [crypto.randomBytes, base64url]
    L->>U: beforeCreate → subscriber.subscribe(sid)  ← BEFORE the row exists
    L->>R: createSession.lua  (state=IDLE, TTL 120s, resumeHash indexed)
    L->>R: setNickname (drawn ONCE, session-scoped, D50)
    L->>R: connAcquire(ipHash, sid)
    alt slot refused
        L->>R: closeSession  ← rollback, no matchable ghost
        L-->>U: too_many_connections → 429
    end
    U->>B: 101 + Set-Cookie kbb_ct (if a client token was issued)
    U->>U: attach(ws, ...)  → registry.add
    U->>R: setAccount + stampEntitlement (fire-and-forget, if signed in)
    U-->>B: connected {sessionId, limits, features, resumeToken, resumeGraceSeconds}
    U-->>B: presence {online, conversations, approximate: true}
